# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_quota_paused_note.py" "QUOTA PAUSED NOTE GATE: PASS" "quota paused note" "early-access fair-use wall is VISIBLE: when an account crosses the free early-access line the DB gate refuses further writes and the graph goes stale, and a PR opened over the wall now posts an ADVISORY 'Veripsa paused — early-access limit reached' check ('neutral', NEVER blocking/failing) + PR comment IN PLACE of the now-stale verdict (the verdict is withheld over a stale graph). The note is content-free + jargon-clean + overclaim-free (same denylist/overclaim scanners every surface holds) and IDEMPOTENT (a re-delivered/synchronize event PATCHES in place — no second comment, no flap). The limit moment is a VISIBLE event, not a silent break, and it does not point to checkout." "early-access fair-use wall visibility (over-line PR posts the advisory limit note instead of a silent stale break; advisory + content-free + jargon-clean + idempotent + verdict-withheld)" 16
